<article class="env-lemma" id="0678">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0678">Lemma <span data-tag="0678">15.83.10</span>.</a> Let $R \to A$ be a finite type ring map. Let $m \in \mathbf{Z}$. Let $K^\bullet \in D^{-}(A)$ such that $H^ i(K^\bullet )$ is $(m - i)$-pseudo-coherent (resp. pseudo-coherent) relative to $R$ for all $i$. Then $K^\bullet $ is $m$-pseudo-coherent (resp. pseudo-coherent) relative to $R$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Immediate from Lemma <a href="/tag/066B" data-tag="066B">15.66.10</a> and the definitions. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>